+## Version 2.0 notes
+
+Dashboard v2.0 (Module 29) = v1.4 + the version number on the screen + automatic tests. The other screens and behavior don't change, the data contract stays 1.6, and no new API route is used. The jump 1.4.0 → 2.0.0 follows the PROJECT number (the backend and the dashboard are both 2.0.0): MAJOR because the way of deploying changed (the images are built by the robot, the VPS and the Pi pull them from GHCR), not because the dashboard changed.
+
+- `package.json` and `package-lock.json`: `version` 2.0.0; a new devDependency `vitest` **5.0.5** (an exact version, installed with `npm install -D -E vitest@5.0.5`; 17 new developer packages in the lock, no new production package); a new script `test` (`vitest run`).
+- New files: `src/time.test.ts`, `src/csv.test.ts`, `src/rules.test.ts` (five tests), `src/version.d.ts`.
+- `vite.config.ts`: the version number is read from `package.json` (`readFileSync`) and written into the JavaScript (`define: { __WEB_VERSION__ }`), not from `npm_package_version` (that variable only exists when Vite is started through `npm run`); a comment about Vitest.
+- `src/pages/Login.tsx` and `src/components/Layout.tsx`: `v2.0.0` under the title. In the dashboard header it's under the title on purpose, not next to it: on a 375 px phone, the title + the number + the badge **Reconnecting…** don't fit on one row, and the title folds into two rows (tried by the author).
+- `Dockerfile`: the `build` stage `FROM --platform=$BUILDPLATFORM node:24.22.1-alpine3.24` (two-processor images without QEMU), comments (the 2.0.0 tag, the `source` label filled in by the robot). `.dockerignore`: `src/**/*.test.ts`.
+- `README.md`: the new sections **Automatic tests (Module 29)** and **The version number (Module 29)**, **Limits of v2.0**, and these notes.
 
